notes: |
  Six rounds, because rounds 2, 3 and 4 each found defects inside the previous
  round's fix. That pattern was the real finding: three facts - the core is not
  answering, the core refused this query, this flow's fetch produced nothing -
  were encoded in two values with precedence baked into the encoding, so each fix
  traded one wrong state for another. Round 4 split them into silent, refused and
  failed with one owner each and moved precedence into the renderers; round 5
  found the build had still invented a ranking between silence and a refusal that
  the run never made; round 6 returned clean by case analysis, proving the band
  and the row region structurally mutually exclusive, and rows-present-with-a-
  refusal unreachable because every path that sets a refusal empties the rows in
  the same update.
  13 verified across the rounds: a latched pane failure speaking for the list,
  never expiring, and a straggling refresh un-doing a retry (r1); the listing
  counter clearing a pane failure without re-fetching, and no zone stating a pane
  failure with the list empty (r2); a second warn for one cause, the stream
  overwriting a refusal, a focus claim that never expired, a stale test title
  (r3); the pane reverting to a false "loading" when the core went silent after
  it had already failed, and a refusal latched through a real outage (r4); an
  invented precedence hiding a refusal, a refusal quoting a value never asked,
  and a trailing clause false of the region below (r5).
  Refuted and recorded as refuted rather than silently acted on: the three
  test-double factories in useFlows.test.ts and shellApi-vs-mockApi in
  App.test.tsx (both follow those files' existing one-double-per-concern
  convention; merging them yields a config object with five knobs, which the
  reuse dimension explicitly excludes); the retry's unconditional nonce bump (the
  design's "one cause, one retry", costing one idempotent GET on a rare
  user-initiated click); the pane still reading "loading this flow..." as judged
  at round 1 (the run puts that sentence in A-prime by design - superseded by
  rounds 3-5, which is why the pane has its own line now); and a duplicated
  comment.
  Recorded, not fixed: a 5xx listing is read as silence, because a core answering
  with a server error leaves the rows exactly as unverified, which is what the
  sentence is for; and the pane's "could not load this flow" also covers a
  ring-dropped flow, whose precise sentence the run reserved as "no longer
  captured".
  Gate 0 green at every round. Final: 831 unit/integration, e2e 32/32,
  onboarding.spec.ts unedited and green.
